	(text "v0.5 Changelog (aka v1.0)\n——————————————————————\n- Added a location for the Wi-Fi Module\n- Changed J2 to support +5V for the Wi-Fi Module\n- Changed the artwork a bit and side up/down text."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 201.93 88.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0dfd07ad-7704-442a-88db-124050165117")
	)
	(text "CL = (C8 * C9)/(C8 + C9) + Cstray\n(324pF/36pF) + 4pF = 13pF\n(close to 12pF Y1 CL requirement)\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 144.78 158.75 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1ac3cb9a-b5f1-4d2e-ac30-58dfd6a4d2c4")
	)
	(text "v0.3 Changelog\n——————————————————————\n- Fixed PCB fingers (removed soldermask ink around fingers, made them 8.8mm\n   x 1.52mm, spaced 1.2mm from board edge, and 18.0mm from 3.6mm hole)\n- Increased hole sizes to 3.7mm, 4.2mm, 5.2mm\n- Made all pads on addressable LEDs the same size\n- Remove D8 - D13, spacing remaining 4 LEDs evenly (13mm)\n- Change debugging header to 3-pin\n- Add 3-pin header to output LED signals (drive 1000’s of LEDs if you want)\n- Added SW1 for programming, and SW2 for STM32 reset\n- Changed C13 from 47uF to 10uF\n- Added cut & solder jumper to convert SW2 to a User Button\n- Added test points for main voltage rails\n- Connected Vectrex 5V directly to PA10\n- Connected V-OE to PB10, changed U3 to single OR gate, and added R7 for\n   optional way to assert U4 /OE in the future potentially."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 201.93 46.99 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "46a79d5a-fdb5-4fde-8daf-c3b0fa5e3de8")
	)
	(text "/E"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.366 106.172 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "54084b77-7723-41de-b193-ddf4382946f7")
	)
	(text "v0.4 Changelog\n——————————————————————\n- Increased length of SW2 to 12mm (TS-1002S-12026C)\n- Changed SW1 to be the same as SW2\n- Replaced J2 & J3 with a single 2x3 header that presses into place and holds\n   itself for soldering. Can use two separate 1x3 headers if desired.\n- Replaced JP1 with a 1x2 header that presses into place for soldering.\n- Added a micro 10-pin JTAG debugging header that doubles as USB Serial\n   adapter as well.\n- Added a solderable jumper on V-NMI to be connected to one of PA8, which \n   also can be optionally connected to SW2.\n- Added a diode for reverse polarity (cart upside down) on VEC_5V detect line.\n- Added a “this side up” label."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 201.93 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8de0aee4-8c31-4af5-a59d-57f969c50edb")
	)
	(text "JP2 normally connected (1-2) for SW2 to\nact as hard reset for STM32.  If (1-2) cut\nand (2-3) soldered SW2 will be connected\nto pull PA8 low (should enable internal\npull-up) to use."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 130.81 172.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c5ca854c-cd4e-45c5-9ade-d4d2da9bd489")
	)
	(text "A15"
